WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
I'm very glad to share that a grand total
of zero of our clients that we set up

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.860
with Paraguayan residency got caught in the
collapse of Ueno, one of Paraguay's

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.700
largest banks that affected almost 50 % of
its population.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.880
Now the reason why none of our clients got
caught up in it is because they weren't

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.580
simply banking in Paraguay.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.060
I really want to distinguish the difference
between setting up residency in

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.320
Paraguay and then the banking layer of
things.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.820
So I thought I'd hop on here and tell you
the best practices that we found and the

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.840
structure that we get our clients set up
with.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.820
So this is how to bank with Paraguayan
residency.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.220
So it's important to distinguish two
different things.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.400
First you have your company banking, which
is set up alongside your US LLC.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.440
The way that I like to think of it is it's
a hub of all your money.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.380
It's where you earn your money into.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.060
It's where you invest your money.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.020
And it's where you save your money and you
save your money there because in the US

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.960
they have really generous deposit insurance
limits or amounts

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:04.360
where you can have millions or hundreds of
thousands depending on the bank parked

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.400
in the bank account.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.560
And it's 100 % deposit insured, whereas in
Paraguay with the collapse of Ueno,

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.220
they only covered up to US $35 ,000.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.660
And then you have your another layer, which
is your personal banking.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.340
These are bank accounts that you'll set up
alongside your Paraguayan residency

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.500
documentation. And again, all overseas,
international, neo banks,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.520
multi currency.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.880
And this is where you do your day to day
spending.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.700
So the coffee that you're going to buy
tomorrow, the pizza that you're going to

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.760
eat tonight, you would pay for that on your
personal banking, but then all of your

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.040
income you earn into the company banking.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:45.080
So again, I think that the number one tip
here is having multiple

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.740
overseas accounts, both at the personal and
at the corporate level.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.540
So let's get into it a bit more.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.980
First of all, focus on the company banking
side of things.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:01.600
So as for company banking, step one is you
want to open a US business account for

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.500
your US LLC.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.120
The ones that we've partnered with and have
special treatment with are Mercury.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.960
You can also open up accounts with Chase
and Slash, and we do this for you in week

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.060
one. So as soon as you on board with us, we
get your US LLC and your banking set

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.880
up straight away so that you can start
earning, investing and saving your money

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.760
as soon as possible.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.520
Then the second thing that you want to do,
and this isn't obligatory, but assuming

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.140
that you want to start to invest your
money, whether that be in stocks, ETF

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.420
bonds,

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.340
crypto,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.920
you would open up investment accounts in
the company name with your US LLC.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:42.180
So that, for an example, is Interactive
Brokers or Coinbase on the crypto side.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.320
But you can use Kraken, you can use Gemini,

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:49.120
all of these support US LLC business
account setups.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.160
And thirdly, you want to redirect your
income to these bank accounts so that your

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:54.880
clients,

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.480
whether that just be if you're a
freelancer, you have multiple clients, or

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:04.050
if you just have one, or if you're earning
money from from Stripe,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.430
you want to redirect all this income to
these bank accounts that you set up, the

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.110
Chase, the Mercury or the Slash.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.430
Again, these are in the US, they aren't in
Paraguay, so they're not affected by

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.670
the collapse of Ueno.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:23.150
And that way, your client pays the company,
and it's not you yourself.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.730
And then at that moment, you decide with
all this money coming into your US LLC

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.270
bank account, you can either invest it or
you can save it.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.030
And as for spending all of it,

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:39.630
you want to be transferring the money from
your US LLC to your personal bank

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.330
accounts, which we'll get into now.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.410
And then from here, you do your general
spending.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:51.830
So you want to open a spending account that
gives you US and EU bank details so

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.430
that you can accept euros, dollars, or a
bunch of different currencies that you

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:59.970
want. And you get a either a virtual or
physical at times both

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:05.230
card with really competitive ATM withdrawal
fees,

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.290
foreign exchange fees, international
spending fees, because we understand that

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.250
most of our customers are remote, multi
based workers who are traveling between

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:18.210
different countries. So the banks that
we've cooperated with and done the research

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.750
on and spoken to are all very nomad
friendly banks.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:24.310
So for example, GetMeru and Bilderlings.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.910
Those are two that you can set up pretty
quickly with your Paraguayan identity and

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.090
even with your passport,

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.070
not with your old tax residency.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:38.130
And yeah, we have a guide where we break
down all the different banks that

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.490
we know work with Paraguayan residency.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:44.810
And they will have different perks to them
and all have different limitations.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.650
If you want that, we can send that over to
you as well.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:52.890
And as well, if you want a real bank with
deposit protection and a more premium

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:57.350
service, well, then you add a premium
option, you can set up a Xapo bank.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:02.570
So Xapo is a bank in Gibraltar that is more
crypto focused, but still has all

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.310
the USD banking rails that you want.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:09.010
You can set up with Chase Bank, a personal
bank account, or even SOLO in Georgia,

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.790
where you have your own personal banker.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.470
And then they have heaps of additional
services like lounge access,

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:17.910
you know, all the good stuff.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.690
They have few tiers depending on what you
want.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:25.750
So SOLO Bank is emerging as a really
popular bank in 2026 for digital nomads.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:29.630
And then from these different bank accounts
on the personal side, this is where

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.650
you do your spending, your coffee, your
food, your flights,

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:36.570
everything you do yourself happens here on
these accounts.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:43.270
And one doubt that people come to us is,
hey, why can't I just use Wise or

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:47.870
Revolut? Well, that's because Wise and
Revolut, neither all accept Paraguayan

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.970
residency in the personal details.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.210
You may have seen these banks are asking
you for tax ID information.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:56.970
Well, as of today, their services are more
regional to Europe.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.650
And they have a couple of other
jurisdictions around the globe.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.750
But as for Paraguay, they don't support
them.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:05.570
So that's why we that's why I mentioned the
banks above because we've gone in

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.350
contact, we've spoken to all these banks.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:12.150
And we know they're Paraguayan friendly, or
US LLC friendly on the company side.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:19.550
And yeah, we break down exactly how to get
set up in Paraguay with this banking

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.070
structure in our $7 masterclass.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:25.070
And with that, you also get a free banking
guide.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:29.710
So you can either tap below or comment
masterclass and we'll send it over to you.
